    "content": "High Point University (HPU) is a private, Methodist-affiliated liberal arts institution in North Carolina, renowned as the #1 \"Best-Run College\" by The Princeton Review (2025, 2026). Known for focusing on life skills, experiential learning, and career readiness, it offers over 70 undergraduate majors and boasts a 99% placement rate. Key Information Location: High Point, NC Enrollment: Approximately 6,550+ students Type: Private Liberal Arts University Focus: \"Life Skills\" university, emphasizing innovation, character development, and career preparation Campus: Known for being highly landscaped, often ranked among the most beautiful in the country Academic & Rankings Rankings: Frequently ranked #1 Regional College in the South, most innovative school, and top for undergraduate teaching by U.S. News & World Report. Programs: Offers 73 undergraduate majors and 70 minors. Academics: Comprised of seven professional schools and a College of Arts and Sciences. Campus Life & Athletics Athletics: The HPU Panthers compete in NCAA Division I athletics (Big South Conference) in 17 varsity sports. Facilities: Ranked #2 for best college dorms and top-tier athletic facilities. Campus Vibe: Known as a \"premier life skills university,\" focusing on holistic student growth and career preparedness. Admissions Acceptance Rate: Approximately 75-76%. Selectivity: Considered moderately competitive. Under President Nido Qubein, the university has undergone rapid expansion, transforming from a small institution to a sprawling 560-acre campus.",
